IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art26-commencement`

-- je21-tests-art26-commencement: tests for Article 26 and the endnotes that say when the Law came into force.
-- The expected values were written by hand from Article 26 and the endnotes' Table of Legislation History (the Law in force on 28 September 2021)
-- and from endnote [2] (Article 2(1) revised on 11 January 2024), before the module was run.

§ `Article 26 -- tests`

§§ `Names for the readings and the times`

`L3 default` MEANS `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)`
`L3 refuse` MEANS `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`
`midnight` MEANS `Time of day` OF 0, 0
`noon` MEANS `Time of day` OF 12, 0
`a minute before midnight` MEANS `Time of day` OF 23, 59

§§ `The day and the endnotes' record`

#ASSERT `Article 26: the day on which the Law came into force` EQUALS YMD 2021 9 28
#ASSERT `Article 26: the commencement of the Law, as the endnotes record it` EQUALS "28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021), the day specified by Act of the States under Article 26"

§§ `In force at some time on the day`

#ASSERT NOT `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` (YMD 2021 9 27)
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` (YMD 2021 9 28)
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` (YMD 2021 9 29)
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` (YMD 2024 1 10)
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` (YMD 2024 1 11)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 26: the Law was in force at some time on the day` (YMD 2000 1 1)

§§ `In force at a time of day on the day`

-- The day before: no, on either reading.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 26: the Law was in force at a time of day on the day` (YMD 2021 9 27) `a minute before midnight` `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 26: the Law was in force at a time of day on the day` (YMD 2021 9 27) `a minute before midnight` `L3 refuse`
-- The day itself: from the beginning of the day on the default reading, refused on the other.
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at a time of day on the day` (YMD 2021 9 28) `midnight` `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at a time of day on the day` (YMD 2021 9 28) `noon` `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at a time of day on the day` (YMD 2021 9 28) `a minute before midnight` `L3 default`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 26: the Law was in force at a time of day on the day` (YMD 2021 9 28) `noon` `L3 refuse` BECAUSE "the sources do not say at what time of day on 28 September 2021 the Law came into force, so whether it was in force at a given time of day that day cannot be answered"
-- The day after: yes, on either reading.
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at a time of day on the day` (YMD 2021 9 29) `midnight` `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 26: the Law was in force at a time of day on the day` (YMD 2021 9 29) `midnight` `L3 refuse`

§§ `Which text governs`

#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2021 9 27) EQUALS `the Law was not in force`
#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2000 1 1) EQUALS `the Law was not in force`
#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2021 9 28) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`
#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2021 9 29) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`
#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2023 12 31) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`
#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2024 1 10) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`
#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2024 1 11) EQUALS `the text of 11 January 2024`
#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2024 1 12) EQUALS `the text of 11 January 2024`
#ASSERT `Article 26 and the endnotes: which text of the Law governs on the day` (YMD 2026 10 27) EQUALS `the text of 11 January 2024`
